Package: PEhub
Title: Promoter-Centric Detection of Multi-Way Enhancer Hubs from Chromatin Interaction Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiang", "Tan", email = "jiangtan@wustl.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Yidan", "Sun", email = "syidan@wustl.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: PEhub reconstructs multi-way enhancer hubs from pairwise chromatin
    interaction data (e.g., H3K27ac HiChIP) by modelling enhancer-promoter
    interactions as promoter-anchored weighted networks, quantifying enhancer
    co-membership, partitioning enhancers into candidate hubs by Leiden community
    detection, and evaluating hubs against a distance-matched null model. The
    Python leidenalg backend is provisioned automatically via basilisk, so no
    manual Python configuration is required.
